{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/822709-primordial-pathways-and-resonance","id":822709,"title":"Primordial Pathways and Resonance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-03T13:53:35-08:00","id":822709,"title":"Primordial Pathways and Resonance","content":"So in a nWoD game I'm playing in, I am currently playing as a Beast. I was trying to determine whether or not I could open a Primordial Pathway to a specific location. In order to determine this, I consulted the rules:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts can\u2019t simply open Pathways between any realms they choose. As with many aspects of their Lair, it\u2019s the resonance, or similarity, between the Lair and somewhere else that affords access. </div> </div> </div>Okay. So there has to be a resonance or similarity between my Chamber and the location. Right. So I can't open one just anywhere?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Opening a Pathway to the exact location from which the Beast created a Chamber is easiest, but desperate Beasts and cunning would-be intruders can use similar locations by spending a point of Willpower during the attempt and incurring an additional dice penalty based on how well the location matches. </div> </div> </div>... Ah. So I *can* open one here, but I take a dice penalty for it not matching. I then turn to the chart on which the dice modifiers can be found.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> DICE MODIFIERS:<br /> +1 The external end of the Pathway is the physical location corresponding to the Chamber in which the Beast is located.<br /> +1 The external end of the Pathway is under the effect of a Lair Trait. Multiple Traits (including those imposed by the Beast by using Lair resonance) apply this bonus on a cumulative basis.<br /> +1 The external end of the Pathway is in the Primordial Dream (e.g., another Beast\u2019s Lair, the nightmares of an unDevoured Beast, or an unclaimed Chamber.)<br /> 0 The external end of the Pathway is in the Temenos.<br /> \u20131 The external end of the Pathway is in the Anima Mundi or Oneiros.<br /> \u20132 The external end of the Pathway is in the Shadow, Hedge, or Underworld.<br /> \u20133 The external end of the Pathway is in the material world (other than the area corresponding to the Chamber).<br /> \u20133 The character has specified a world, but not a precise location. </div> </div> </div>So this chart doesn't actually give any modifiers based on the resonance or similarity of a location to the Chamber you are trying to open a Pathway to. Which means, so as far as I can tell, it doesn't actually matter whether a location resonates with your Lair or not for opening a Primordial Pathway there. It matters for manifesting Lair Traits, but not for actually opening the Pathway... which seems altogether weird. Am I missing something here? <br /> <br /> Also, if I am in my Lair, can I target any location as the external end of the Primordial Pathway? Only locations I have personally visited? Could I open a Primordial Pathway to Fort Knox? The White House? Buckingham Palace? 10 Downing Street? Tokyo Tower? Hoover Dam? To manor of the Feathered King in the courts of the Gentle Folk? To the fortress of Osiris in the depths of the Underworld?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:08:18-08:00","id":822732,"title":"","content":"As far as I understand it, the external end needs to have resonance with the Lair. That is, it must possess at least one of the Lair's Traits. I think. I don't think you can just open a Pathway wherever you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T16:59:56-08:00","id":822887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> pg 101</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In a location used to create one of her Chambers, a Beast<br /> may pay a point of Satiety to impose any of her Lair Traits up<br /> to the limit of Traits per scene without needing the initial Tilt.<br /> <b>As with opening a Primordial Pathway, Beasts may attempt to<br /> use a Chamber in locations that are similar, if not exactly the<br /> same, by spending a Willpower point.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So the implication here is that you need at least some similarity to be able to open the pathway with a point of willpower. Potentially harder as the similarities listed on pg 102 gives the chart that goes up to a -5 for attempting to handle it with an area that matches up only on the idea of two forests being interchangeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T17:09:59-08:00","id":822894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/822709-primordial-pathways-and-resonance?p=822887#post822887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the implication here is that you need at least some similarity to be able to open the pathway with a point of willpower. Potentially harder as the similarities listed on pg 102 gives the chart that goes up to a -5 for attempting to handle it with an area that matches up only on the idea of two forests being interchangeable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, this helps. I didn't actually think to read all the way to the page you quoted for the dice modifiers on Primordial Pathways -- I assumed that the relevant rules would all be in the section that described actually opening Primordial Pathways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Hige sceal \u00fe\u0113 heardra, heorte \u00fe\u0113 c\u0113nre,<br /> m\u014dd sceal \u00fe\u0113 m\u0101re, \u00fe\u0113 \u016bre m\u00e6gen lytla\u00f0.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8950-vithrir","name":"Vithrir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}